d she says hello so what do we think  makes sense for what happened - L see  I've been reading different things and I  went back and I watched some different  scenes with her in it I mean there's no  doubt about it they set her up to be an  important character she's right below  Bernard who is Ford's right-hand man it  just doesn't make sense that they would  build the characters up and then have  them die sort of unceremoniously  off-screen there's actually an article  that came out in Entertainment Weekly  where the two show runners were asked  the question directly  the interviewer points out that both of  them could have been useful in this end  part especially Stubbs whenever it came  to the uprising and Jonathan Nolan and  Lisa joy answered like this look we  loved working with Luke and Shannon they  were early incarnations where we tied up  those arcs in the finale  I'm not saying how I'm just saying we  tied them up I wouldn't say tied them up  I would say we unspooled them in an  uncertain future where we elucidated  their fate more explicitly but their  fates we know where they're going and  we'll get them there Nolan finishes by  saying we dearly love both those actors  we also you know it was not our  intention to spend out huge mysteries ad  infinitum we wanted to resolve some  pretty important storytelling but we  didn't want to answer every question so  going back and rewatching some of the LC  scenes as they relate to knowing that  Ford was actually trying to have the  host wake up and be able to stand on  their own she was actually a pretty  important character on first watch she  just seems like she's there to push  things along with Bernard but there are  a couple times when you can tell that  she actually has a real interest in the  host development I mean it's it's  superficially about how they are in the  park but she's clearly smarter than the  average person about how things work and  then there's a couple weird scenes that  don't make any sense  like when she kisses Clementine in the  first episode and then later she seems  to feel real sympathy for the Loras in  that scene in the street before she puts  her in sleep mode she also  seems to be really competent and  probably is the third most useful coder  after Bernard and Ford himself so we're  all familiar with the scene with Bernard  choking her and I think there's a real  possibility that Ford was being honest  whenever he said that he never had  Bernard hurt anyone else like that all  we see is him choke her if Ford did have  him kill her he could have just told  Bernard about it and then rolled him  back the reveries themself is what  brought that memory back so Ford might  not have realized that that was what was  causing Bernard the trouble either way  there's a couple scenarios where she  doesn't die at the end of that the first  which I think makes the most sense is  that she was just being put in a  chokehold that was supposed to knock her  out not kill her the second would be  that she realized when she was looking  at the tablet before he got there that  he was actually a host and then was able  to use voice commands to stop him those  would have two different outcomes of  course I mean if she stopped him with  voice commands then she probably escaped  into the park somewhere but if he choked  her out then she was probably put  somewhere for safekeeping  one thing that I checked when I was  watching is that a lot of people asked  in the comments wasn't she on the phone  with him right before she got choked and  the answer is no if you go back and  watch that episode you'll see that they  end their phone conversation with her  saying that she's gonna download the  rest of the information and then meet  him at his office then it cuts to a  different scene and there would have  been plenty of times for him to get  there and to choke her out I think that  takes off the option of it being Arnold  and not Bernard because I think that the  finale